course: dictionary
lesson: 1698
title: Chunky: thick, solid or unkind?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so context tells you which one you need. «She pulled on her chunky knit jumper before going out into the snow.» The clues are the jumper and the snow, so chunky means thick and warm, not fat.
explain: «The soup was full of chunky carrots and potatoes.» Here chunky means containing thick pieces. The food words are the clue. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Chunky can also describe a person or animal who is short and broad. This is informal, and it can hurt someone's feelings. «Chunky» often means fat, especially of a child, so think carefully before you use it about a person.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Chunky» means thick, solid and heavy-looking, as in a chunky jumper or chunky boots.
fact: «Chunky» can mean containing thick pieces, as in chunky soup or chunky peanut butter.
fact: «Chunky» can describe a person or animal who is short and broad, but this is informal and can be unkind.
fact: Chunky knit and chunky chips are useful phrases; in art, chunky lines are thick.
exercise: «She pulled on her chunky knit jumper before going out into the snow.» What does chunky mean here? | Fast and light | Torn and dirty | *Thick and warm, with a solid look | Very quiet
exercise: «The soup was full of chunky carrots and potatoes.» What does chunky suggest? | Very salty | Hidden under the bowl | *Containing thick pieces | Cold and smooth
exercise: Mia says «chunky» always means fat. What is the best answer? | *It can mean thick or solid, and calling a person chunky can be unkind | It means very fast | It means very small | It always means fat, so use it freely about anyone
test: «The boots were chunky, so they kept his feet warm in the snow.» What does chunky mean here? | Very quiet | Thin and light | *Thick and solid | Cold and wet
test: Which is the safest way to use chunky about a person? | As another word for skinny | To describe the strongest person in the team | *Only in a kind way, and never to hurt someone's feelings | To tease a friend about their weight
exam: Which sentence uses chunky to mean containing thick pieces? | Dad wore a thin shirt to work | The room was dark and quiet | *Dad made chunky peanut butter sandwiches for lunch | Mum ran very fast to catch the bus
